20zx|v|To feel, or endure, with pain, annoyance, etc.; to submit to with distress or grief; to undergo; as, to suffer pain of body, or grief of mind. ; To endure or undergo without sinking; to support; to sustain; to bear up under. ; To undergo; to be affected by; to sustain; to experience; as, most substances suffer a change when long exposed to air and moisture; to suffer loss or damage. ; To allow; to permit; not to forbid or hinder; to tolerate. ; To feel or undergo pain of body or mind; to bear what is inconvenient; as, we suffer from pain, sickness, or sorrow; we suffer with anxiety. ; To undergo punishment; specifically, to undergo the penalty of death. ; To be injured; to sustain loss or damage.	s:20bd,33,6~20bd,33,6
