215l|n|The aggregate of two or more numbers, magnitudes, quantities, or particulars; the amount or whole of any number of individuals or particulars added together; as, the sum of 5 and 7 is 12. ; A quantity of money or currency; any amount, indefinitely; as, a sum of money; a small sum, or a large sum. ; The principal points or thoughts when viewed together; the amount; the substance; compendium; as, this is the sum of all the evidence in the case; this is the sum and substance of his objections. ; Height; completion; utmost degree. ; A problem to be solved, or an example to be wrought out.	a:168q,65,10~168q,65,10
